he last expression are returned.") ("If the first clause whose " (code (var "test")) " evaluates to a true value is in the third form given above, the expression " (code (var "expr")) " is evaluated. The value should be a procedure of one argument, which is applied to the value of " (code (var "test")) ". The values of this application are returned.") ("If none of the tests evaluates to a true value and an " (code "else") " clause is present, the expressions " (code (var "expr" (sub "1")) " " (var "expr" (sub "2")) " ...") " of the " (code "else") "  clause are evaluated in sequence and the values of the last expression are returned.") ("If none of the tests evaluates to a true value and no " (code "else") " clause is present, the value or values are unspecified.") ("See page " (link "./syntax.html#defn:cond" "305") " for a syntax definition of " (code "cond") ".") ((code "(let ([x 0])" (br) "  (cond" (br) "    [(< x 0) (list 'minus (abs x))]" (br) "    [(> x 0) (list 'plus x)]" (br) "    [else (list 'zero x)])) " (math "=>") " (zero 0)" (br) (br) "(define select" (br) "  (lambda (x)" (br) "    (cond" (br) "      [(not (symbol? x))]" (br) "      [(assq x '((a . 1) (b . 2) (c . 3))) => cdr]" (br) "      [else 0])))" (br) (br) "(select 3) " (math "=>") " #t" (br) "(select 'b) " (math "=>") " 2" (br) "(select 'e) " (math "=>") " 0"))) ("control:s16" ((bold "syntax") ": " (code "else") (br) (bold "syntax") ": " (code "=>") (br) (bold "libraries: ") (code "(rnrs base)") ", " (code "(rnrs exceptions)") ", " (code "(rnrs)")) ("These identifiers are auxiliary keywords for " (code "cond") ". Both also serve as auxiliary keywords for " (code "guard") ", and " (code "else") " also serves as an auxiliary keyword for " (code "case") ". It is a syntax violation to reference these identifiers except in contexts where they are recognized as auxiliary keywords.")) ("control:s17" ((bold "syntax") ": " (code "(when " (var "test-expr") " " (var "expr" (sub "1")) " " (var "expr" (sub "2