d to zero length. If the " (code "no-create") " option is included, the file is not created if it does not exist; instead, an exception is raised with condition type " (code "i/o-file-does-not-exist") ". The " (code "no-create") " option implies the " (code "no-fail") " option. The " (code "no-truncate") " option is relevant only if the " (code "no-fail") "  option is included or implied, in which case if an existing file is opened, it is not truncated, but the port's position is still set to the beginning of the file.") ("It is perhaps easier to imagine that the default file options are the imaginary option symbols " (code "create") ", " (code "fail-if-exists") ", and " (code "truncate") "; " (code "no-create") " removes " (code "create") ", " (code "no-fail") " removes " (code "fail-if-exists") ", and " (code "no-truncate") " removes " (code "truncate") ".") ("Implementations may support additional file option symbols. Chez Scheme, for example, supports options that control whether the file is or should be compressed, whether it is locked for exclusive access, and what permissions are given to the file if it is created [" (link "./bibliography.html#g227" "9") "].")) ("io:s27" ((bold "syntax") ": " (code "(buffer-mode " (var "symbol") ")") (br) (bold "returns: ") (code (var "symbol")) (br) (bold "libraries: ") (code "(rnrs io ports)") ", " (code "(rnrs)")) ((code (var "symbol")) " must be one of the symbols " (code "block") ", " (code "line") ", or " (code "none") ". The expression " (code "(buffer-mode " (var "symbol") ")") " is equivalent to the expression " (code "(quote " (var "symbol") ")") " except that the former checks at expansion time that " (code (var "symbol")) " is one of the buffer-mode symbols. The " (code "buffer-mode") " syntax provides useful documentation as well.") ((code "(buffer-mode block) " (math "=>") " block" (br) "(buffer-mode cushion) " (math "=>") " " (var "syntax violation")))) ("io:s28" ((bold "syntax") ": " (code "(buffer-mode? " (var "obj") ")") (br) (bold "returns: ") (code "#t") " if " (code (var "obj")) " is a valid buffer mode, " (code "#f") " otherwise" (br) (bold "libraries: ") (code "(rnrs io ports)") ", " (code "(rnrs)")) ((code "(buffer-mode? 'block) " (math "=>") " #t" (br) "(buffer-mode? 'line) " (math "=>") " #t" (br) "(buffer-mode? 'none) " (math "=>") " #t" (br) "(buffer-mode? 'something-else) " (math "=>") " #f"))) ("io:s29" ((bold "procedure") ": " (code "(open-file-input-port " (var "path") ")") (br) (bold "procedure") ": " (code "(open-file-input-port " (var "path") " " (var "options") ")") (br) (bold "procedure") ": " (code "(open-file-input-port " (var "path") " " (var "options") " " (var "b-mode") ")") (br) (bold "procedure") ": " (code "(open-file-input-port " (var "path") " " (var "options") " " (var "b-mode") " " (var "?transcoder") ")") (br) (bold "returns: ") "a new input port for the named file" (br) (bold "libraries: ") (code "(rnrs io ports)") ", " (code "(rnrs)")) ("If " (code (var "?transcoder")) " is present and not " (code "#f") ", it must be a transcoder, and this procedure returns a textual input port whose transcoder is " (code (var "?transcoder")) ". Otherwise, this procedure returns a binary input port. See the lead-in to this section for a description of the constraints on and effects of the other arguments.")) ("io:s30" ((bold "procedure") ": " (code "(open-file-output-port " (var "path") ")") (br) (bold "procedure") ": " (code "(open-file-output-port " (var "path") " " (var "options") ")") (br) (bold "procedure") ": " (code "(open-file-output-port " (var "path") " " (var "options") " " (var "b-mode") ")") (br) (bold "procedure") ": " (code "(open-file-output-port " (var "path") " " (var "options") " " (var "b-mode") " " (var "?transcoder") ")") (br) (bold "returns: ") "a new output port for the named file" (br) (bold "libraries: ") (code "(rnrs io ports)") ", " (code "(rnrs)")) ("If " (code (var "?transcoder")) " is present and not " (code "#f") ", it must be a transcoder, and this procedure returns a textual output port whose transcoder is " (code (var "?transcoder")) ". Otherwise, this procedure returns a binary output port. See the lead-in to this section for a description of the constraints on and effects of the other arguments.")) ("io:s31" ((bold "procedure") ": " (code "(open-file-input/output-port " (var "path") ")") (br) (bold "procedure") ": " (code "(open-file-input/output-port " (var "path") " " (var "options") ")") (br) (bold "procedure") ": " (code "(open-file-input/output-port " (var "path") " " (var "options") " " (var "b-mode") ")") (br) (bold "procedure") ": " (code "(open-file-input/output-port " (var "path") " " (var "options") " " (var "b-mode") " " (var "?transcoder") ")") (br) (bold "returns: ") "a new input/output port for the named file" (br) (bold "libraries: ") (code "(rnrs io ports)") ", " (code "(rnrs)")) ("If " (code (var "?transcoder")) " is present and not " (code "#f") ", it must be a transcoder, and this procedure returns a textual input/output port whose transcoder is " (code (var "?transcoder")) ". Otherwise, this procedure returns a binary input/output port. See the lead-in to this section for a description of the constraints on and effects of the other arguments.")) ("io:s32" ((bold "procedure") ": " (code "(current-input-port)") (br) (bold "returns: ") "the current input port" (br) (bold "procedure") ": " (code "(current-output-port)") (br) (bold "returns: ") "the current output port" (br) (bold "procedure") ": " (code "(current-error-port)") (br) (bold "returns: ") "the current error port" (br) (bold "libraries: ") (code "(rnrs io ports)") ", " (code "(rnrs io simple)") ", " (code "(rnrs)")) ("The current-input, current-output, and current-error ports return pre-built textual ports that are initially associated with a process's standard input, standard output, and standard error streams.") ("The values returned by " (code "current-input-port") " and " (code "current-output-port") " can be altered temporarily by the convenience I/O procedures " (code "with-input-from-file") " and " (code "with-output-to-file") "  (Section " (link "./io.html#g130" "7.9") ").")) ("io:s33" ((bold "procedure") ": " (code "(standard-input-port)") (br) (bold "returns: ") "a fresh binary input port connected to the standard input stream" (br) (bold "procedure") ": " (code "(standard-output-port)") (br) (bold "returns: ") "a fresh binary output port connected to the standard output stream" (br) (bold "procedure") ": " (code "(standard-error-port)") (br) (bold "returns: ") "a fresh binary output port connected to the standard error stream" (br) (bold "libraries: ") (code "(rnrs io ports)") ", " (code "(rnrs)")) ("Because ports may be buffered, confusion can result if operations on more than one port attached to one of a process's standard streams are interleaved. Thus, these procedures are typically appropriate only when a program no longer needs to use any existing ports attached to the standard streams.")) ("io:s34" ((bold "procedure") ": " (code "(open-bytevector-input-port " (var "bytevector") ")") (br) (bold "procedure") ": " (code "(open-bytevector-input-port " (var "bytevector") " " (var "?transcoder") ")") (br) (bold "returns: ") "a new input port that draws input from " (code (var "bytevector")) (br) (bold "libraries: ") (code "(rnrs io ports)") ", " (code "(rnrs)")) ("If " (code (var "?transcoder")) " is present and not " (code "#f") ", it must be a transcoder, and this procedure returns a textual input port whose transcoder is " (code (var "?transcoder")) ". Otherwise, this procedure returns a binary input port.") ("The effect of modifying " (code (var "bytevector")) " after this procedure is called is unspecified.") ((code "(let ([ip (open-bytevector-input-port #vu8(1 2))])" (br) "  (let* ([x1 (get-u8 ip)] [x2 (get-u8 ip)] [x3 (get-u8 ip)])" (br) "    (list x1 x2 (eof-object? x3)))) " (math "=>") " (1 2 #t)")) ("There is no need to close a bytevector port; it's storage will be reclaimed automatically when it is no longer needed, as with any other object, and an open bytevector port does not tie up any operating system resources.")) ("io:s35" ((bold "procedure") ": " (code "(open-string-input-port " (var "string") ")") (br) (bold "returns: ") "a new textual input port that draws input from " (code (var "string")) (br) (bold "libraries: ") (code "(rnrs io ports)") ", " (code "(rnrs)")) ("The effect of modifying " (code (var "string")) " after this procedure is called is unspecified. The new port may or may not have a transcoder, and if it does, the transcoder is implementation-dependent. While not required, implementations are encouraged to support " (code "port-position") "  and " (code "set-port-position!") " for string ports.") ((code "(get-line (open-string-input-port \"hi.\\nwhat's up?\\n\")) " (math "=>") " \"hi.\"")) ("There is no need to close a string port; it's storage will be reclaimed automatically when it is no longer needed, as with any other object, and an open string port does not tie up any operating system resources.")) ("io:s36" ((bold "procedure") ": " (code "(open-bytevector-output-port)") (br) (bold "procedure") ": " (code "(open-bytevector-output-port " (var "?transcoder") ")") (br) (bold "returns: ") "two values, a new output port and an extraction procedure" (br) (bold "libraries: ") (code "(rnrs io ports)") ", " (code "(rnrs)")) ("If " (code (var "?transcoder")) " is present and not " (code "#f") ", it must be a transcoder, and the port value is a textual output port whose transcoder is " (code (var "?transcoder")) ". Otherwise, the port value is a binary output port.") ("The extraction procedure is a procedure that, when called without arguments, creates a bytevector containing the accumulated bytes in the port, clears the port of its accumulated bytes, resets its position to zero, and returns the bytevector. The accumulated bytes include any bytes written beyond the end of the current position, if the position has been set back from its maximum extent.") ((code "(let-values ([(op g) (open-bytevector-output-port)])" (br) "  (put-u8 op 15)" (br) "  (put-u8 op 73)" (br) "  (put-u8 op 115)" (br) "  (set-port-position! op 2)" (br) "  (let ([bv1 (g)])" (br) "    (put-u8 op 27)" (br) "    (list bv1 (g)))) " (math "=>") " (#vu8(15 73 115) #vu8(27))")) ("There is no need to close a bytevector port; it's storage will be reclaimed automatically when it is no longer needed, as with any other object, and an open bytevector port does not tie up any operating system resources.")) ("io:s37" ((bold "procedure") ": " (code "(open-string-output-port)") (br) (bold "returns: ") "two values, a new textual output port and an extraction procedure" (br) (bold "libraries: ") (code "(rnrs io ports)") ", " (code "(rnrs)")) ("The extraction procedure is a procedure that, when called without arguments, creates a string containing the accumulated characters in the port, clears the port of its accumulated characters, resets its position to zero, and returns the string. The accumulated characters include any characters written beyond the end of the current position, if the position has been set back from its maximum extent. While not required, implementations are encouraged to support " (code "port-position") "  and " (code "set-port-position!") " for string ports.") ((code "(let-values ([(op g) (open-string-output-port)])" (br) "  (put-string op \"some data\")" (br) "  (let ([str1 (g)])" (br) "    (put-string op \"new stuff\")" (br) "    (list str1 (g)))) " (math "=>") " (\"some data\" \"new stuff\")")) ("There is no need to close a string port; it's storage will be reclaimed automatically when it is no longer needed, as with any other object, and an open string port does not tie up any operating system resources.")) ("io:s38" ((bold "procedure") ": " (code "(call-with-bytevector-output-port " (var "procedure") ")") (br) (bold "procedure") ": " (code "(call-with-bytevector-output-port " (var "procedure") " " (var "?transcoder") ")") (br) (bold "returns: ") "a bytevector containing the accumulated bytes" (br) (bold "libraries: ") (code "(rnrs io ports)") ", " (code "(rnrs)")) ("If " (code (var "?transcoder")) " is present and not " (code "#f") ", it must be a transcoder, and " (code (var "procedure")) " is called with a textual bytevector output port whose transcoder is " (code (var "?transcoder")) ". Otherwise, " (code (var "procedure")) " is called with a binary bytevector output port. If " (code (var "procedure")) " returns, a bytevector containing the bytes accumulated in the port is created, the accumulated bytes are cleared from the port, the port's position is reset to zero, and the bytevector is returned from " (code "call-with-bytevector-output-port") ". These actions occur each time " (code (var "procedure")) " returns, if it returns multiple times due to the invocation of a continuation created while " (code (var "procedure")) " is active.") ((code "(let ([tx (make-transcoder (latin-1-codec) (eol-style lf)" (br) "            (error-handling-mode replace))])" (br) "  (call-with-bytevector-output-port" (br) "    (lambda (p) (put-string p \"abc\"))" (br) "    tx)) " (math "=>") " #vu8(97 98 99)"))) ("io:s39" ((bold "procedure") ": " (code "(call-with-string-output-port " (var "procedure") ")") (br) (bold "returns: ") "a string containing the accumulated characters" (br) (bold "libraries: ") (code "(rnrs io ports)") ", " (code "(rnrs)")) ((code (var "procedure")) " is called with one argument, a string output port. If " (code (var "procedure")) " returns, a string containing the characters accumulated in the port is created, the accumulated characters are cleared from the port, the port's position is reset to zero, and the string is returned from " (code "call-with-string-output-port") ". These actions occur each time " (code (var "procedure")) " returns, if it returns multiple times due to the invocation of a continuation created while " (code (var "procedure")) " is active.") ((code "call-with-string-output-port") " can be used along with " (code "put-datum") " to define a procedure, " (code "object->string") ", that returns a string containing the printed representation of an object.") ((code "(define (object->string x)" (br) "  (call-with-string-output-port" (br) "    (lambda (p) (put-datum p x))))" (br) (br) "(object->string (cons 'a '(b c))) " (math "=>") " \"(a b c)\""))) ("io:s41" ((bold "procedure") ": " (code "(make-custom-binary-input-port " (var "id") " " (var "r!") " " (var "gp") " " (var "sp!") " " (var "close") ")") (br) (bold "returns: ") "a new custom binary input port" (br) (bold "procedure") ": " (code "(make-custom-binary-output-port " (var "id") " " (var "w!") " " (var "gp") " " (var "sp!") " " (var "close") ")") (br) (bold "returns: ") "a new custom binary output port" (br) (bold "procedure") ": " (code "(make-custom-binary-input/output-port " (var "id") " " (var "r!") " " (var "w!") " " (var "gp") " " (var "sp!") " " (var "close") ")") (br) (bold "returns: ") "a new custom binary input/output port" (br) (bold "libraries: ") (code "(rnrs io ports)") ", " (code "(rnrs)")) ("These procedures allow programs to create ports from arbitrary byte streams. " (code (var "id")) " must be a string naming the new port; the name is used for informational purposes only, and an implementation may choose to include it in the printed syntax, if any, of a custom port. " (code (var "r!")) " and " (code (var "w!")) " must be procedures, while " (code (var "gp")) ", " (code (var "sp!")) ", and " (code (var "close")) " must each be a procedure or " (code "#f") ". These arguments are described below.") ((dt (code (var "r!"))) (dd " is called to draw input from the custom port, e.g., to support " (code "get-u8") " or " (code "get-bytevector-n") ". It is called with three arguments: " (code (var "bytevector")) ", " (code (var "start")) ", and " (code (var "n")) ". " (code (var "start")) " will be a nonnegative exact integer, " (code (var "n")) " will be a positive exact integer, and the sum of " (code (var "start")) " and " (code (var "n")) " will not exceed the length of " (code (var "bytevector")) ". If the byte stream is at end of file, " (code (var "r!")) " should return exact 0. Otherwise, it should read at least one and at most " (code (var "n")) " bytes from the stream, store these bytes in consecutive locations of " (code (var "bytevector")) "  starting at " (code (var "start")) ", and return as an exact positive integer the number of bytes actually read.")) ((dt (code (var "w!"))) (dd " is called to send output to the port, e.g., to support " (code "put-u8") " or " (code "put-bytevector") ". It is called with three arguments: " (code (var "bytevector")) ", " (code (var "start")) ", and " (code (var "n")) ". " (code (var "start")) " and " (code (var "n")) " will be nonnegative exact integers, and the sum of " (code (var "start")) " and " (code (var "n")) " will not exceed the length of " (code (var "bytevector")) ". " (code (var "w!")) " should write up to " (code (var "n")) " consecutive bytes from " (code (var "bytevector")) " starting at " (code (var "start")) " and return, as an exact nonnegative integer, the number of bytes actually written.")) ((dt (code (var "gp"))) (dd " is called to query the port's position. If it is " (code "#f") ", the port will not support " (code "port-position") ". If it is not " (code "#f") ", it will be passed zero arguments and should return the current position as a displacement in bytes from the start of the byte stream as an exact nonnegative integer.")) ((dt (code (var "sp!"))) (dd " is called to set the port's position. If it is " (code "#f") ", the port will not support " (code "set-port-position!") ". If it is not " (code "#f") ", it will be passed one argument, an exact nonnegative integer representing the new position as a displacement in bytes from the start of the byte stream, and it should set the position to this value.")) ((dt (code (var "close"))) (dd " is called to close the byte stream. If it is " (code "#f") ", no action will be taken to close the byte stream when the new port is closed. If it is not " (code "#f") ", it will be passed zero arguments and should take whatever actions are necessary to close the byte stream.")) ("If the new port is an input/output port and does not provide either a " (code (var "gp")) " or " (code (var "sp!")) " procedure, it may not be possible for the implementation to position the port properly if an output operation occurs after an input operation, due to input buffering that must be done to support " (code "lookahead-u8") " and is often done anyway for efficiency. For the same reason, a call to " (code "port-position") " after an input operation may not return an accurate position if the " (code (var "sp!")) " procedure is not provided. Thus, programs that create custom binary input/output ports should generally provide both " (code (var "gp")) " and " (code (var "sp!")) " procedures.")) ("io:s42" ((bold "procedure") ": " (code "(make-custom-textual-input-port " (var "id") " " (var "r!") " " (var "gp") " " (var "sp!") " " (var "close") ")") (br) (bold "returns: ") "a new custom textual input port" (br) (bold "procedure") ": " (code "(make-custom-textual-output-port " (var "id") " " (var "w!") " " (var "gp") " " (var "sp!") " " (var "close") ")") (br) (bold "returns: ") "a new custom textual output port" (br) (bold "procedure") ": " (code "(make-custom-textual-input/output-port " (var "id") " " (var "r!") " " (var "w!") " " (var "gp") " " (var "sp!") " " (var "close") ")") (br) (bold "returns: ") "a new custom textual input/output port" (br) (bold "libraries: ") (code "(rnrs io ports)") ", " (code "(rnrs)")) ("These procedures allow programs to create ports from arbitrary character streams. " (code (var "id")) " must be a string naming the new port; the name is used for informational purposes only, and an implementation may choose to include it in the printed syntax, if any, of a custom port. " (code (var "r!")) " and " (code (var "w!")) " must be procedures, while " (code (var "gp")) ", " (code (var "sp!")) ", and " (code (var "close")) " must each be a procedure or " (code "#f") ". These arguments are described below.") ((dt (code (var "r!"))) (dd " is called to draw input from the port, e.g., to support " (code "get-char") " or " (code "get-string-n") ". It is called with three arguments: " (code (var "string")) ", " (code (var "start")) ", and " (code (var "n")) ". " (code (var "start")) " will be a nonnegative exact integer, " (code (var "n")) " will be a positive exact integer, and the sum of " (code (var "start")) " and " (code (var "n")) " will not exceed the length of " (code (var "string")) ". If the character stream is at end of file, " (code (var "r!")) " should return exact 0. Otherwise, it should read at least one and at most " (code (var "n")) " characters from the stream, store these characters in consecutive locations of " (code (var "string")) "  starting at " (code (var "start")) ", and return as an exact positive integer the number of characters actually read.")) ((dt (code (var "w!"))) (dd " is called to send output to the port, e.g., to support " (code "put-char") " or " (code "put-string") ". It is called with three arguments: " (code (var "string")) ", " (code (var "start")) ", and " (code (var "n")) ". " (code (var "start")) " and " (code (var "n")) " will be nonnegative exact integers, and the sum of " (code (var "start")) " and " (code (var "n")) " will not exceed the length of " (code (var "string")) ". " (code (var "w!")) " should write up to " (code (var "n")) " consecutive characters from " (code (var "string")) " starting at " (code (var "start")) " and return, as an exact nonnegative integer, the number of characters actually written.")) ((dt (code (var "gp"))) (dd " is called to query the port's position. If it is " (code "#f") ", the port will not support " (code "port-position") ". If it is not " (code "#f") ", it will be passed zero arguments and should return the current position, which may be an arbitrary value.")) ((dt (code (var "sp!"))) (dd " is called to set the port's position. If it is " (code "#f") ", the port will not support " (code "set-port-position!") ". If it is not " (code "#f") ", it will be passed one argument, " (code (var "pos")) ", a value representing the new position. If " (code (var "pos")) " is the result of a previous call to " (code (var "gp")) ", " (code (var "sp!")) " should set the position to " (code (var "pos")) ".")) ((dt (code (var "close"))) (dd " is called to close the character stream. If it is " (code "#f") ", no action will be taken to close the character stream when the new port is closed. If it is not " (code "#f") ", it will be passed zero arguments and should take whatever actions are necessary to close the character stream.")) ("If the new port is an input/output port, it may not be possible for the implementation to position the port properly if an output operation occurs after an input operation, even if the " (code (var "gp")) " and " (code (var "sp!")) " procedures are provided, due to input buffering that must be done to support " (code "lookahead-char") " and is often done anyway for efficiency. Since the representations of port positions are not specified, it is not possible for the implementation to adjust the " (code (var "gp")) " return value to account for the number of buffered characters. For the same reason, a call to " (code "port-position") " after an input operation may not return an accurate position, even if the " (code (var "sp!")) "  procedure is provided.") ("It should, however, be possible to perform output reliably after reading if the position is reset to the starting position. Thus, programs that create custom textual input/output ports should generally provide both " (code (var "gp")) " and " (code (var "sp!")) " procedures, and consumers of these ports should obtain the starting position via " (code "port-position") " before any input operations and reset the position back to the starting position before doing any output operations.")) ("io:s43" ((bold "procedure") ": " (code "(port? " (var "obj") ")") (br) (bold "returns: ") (code "#t") " if " (code (var "obj")) " is a port, " (code "#f") " otherwise" (br) (bold "libraries: ") (code "(rnrs io ports)") ", " (code "(rnrs)"))) ("io:s44" ((bold "procedure") ": " (code "(input-port? " (var "obj") ")") (br) (bold "returns: ") (code "#t") " if " (code (var "obj")) " is an input or input/output port, " (code "#f") " otherwise" (br) (bold "procedure") ": " (code "(output-port? " (var "obj") ")") (br) (bold "returns: ") (code "#t") " if " (code (var "obj")) " is an output or input/output port, " (code "#f") " otherwise" (br) (bold "libraries: ") (code "(rnrs io ports)") ", " (code "(rnrs io simple)") ", " (code "(rnrs)"))) ("io:s45" ((bold "procedure") ": " (code "(binary-port? " (var "obj") ")") (br) (bold "returns: ") (code "#t") " if " (code (var "obj")) " is a binary port, " (code "#f") " otherwise" (br) (bold "procedure") ": " (code "(textual-port? " (var "obj") ")") (br) (bold "returns: ") (code "#t") " if " (code (var "obj")) " is a textual port, " (code "#f") " otherwise" (br) (bold "libraries: ") (code "(rnrs io ports)") ", " (code "(rnrs)"))) ("io:s46" ((bold "procedure") ": " (code "(close-port " (var "port") ")") (br) (bold "returns: ") "unspecified" (br) (bold "libraries: ") (code "(rnrs io ports)") ", " (code "(rnrs)")) ("If " (code (var "port")) " is not already closed, " (code "close-port") " closes it, first flushing any buffered bytes or characters to the underlying stream if the port is an output port. Once a port has been closed, no more input or output operations may be performed on the port. Because the operating system may place limits on the number of file ports open at one time or restrict access to an open file, it is good practice to close any file port that will no longer be used for input or output. If the port is an output port, closing the port explicitly also ensures that buffered data is written to the underlying stream. Some Scheme implementations close file ports automatically after they become inaccessible to the program or when the Scheme program exits, but it is best to close file ports explicitly whenever possible. Closing a port that has already been closed has no effect.")) ("io:s47" ((bold "procedure") ": " (code "(transcoded-port " (var "binary-port") " " (var "transcoder") ")") (br) (bold "returns: ") "a new textual port with the same byte stream as " (code (var "binary-port")) (br) (bold "libraries: ") (code "(rnrs io ports)") ", " (code "(rnrs)")) ("This procedure returns a new textual port with transcoder " (code (var "transcoder")) "  and the same underlying byte stream as " (code (var "binary-port")) ", positioned at the current position of " (code (var "binary-port")) ".") ("As a side effect of creating the textual port, " (code (var "binary-port")) " is closed to prevent read or write operations on " (code (var "binary-port")) " from interfering with read and write operations on the new textual port. The underlying byte stream remains open, however, until the textual port is closed.")) ("io:s48" ((bold "procedure") ": " (code "(port-transcoder " (var "port") ")") (br) (bold "returns: ") "the transcoder associated with " (code (var "port")) " if any, " (code "#f") " otherwise" (br) (bold "libraries: ") (code "(rnrs io ports)") ", " (code "(rnrs)")) ("This procedure always returns " (code "#f") " for binary ports and may return " (code "#f") " for some textual ports.")) ("io:s49" ((bold "procedure") ": " (code "(port-position " (var "port") ")") (br) (bold "returns: ") "the port's current position" (br) (bold "procedure") ": " (code "(port-has-port-position? " (var "port") ")") (br) (bold "returns: ") (code "#t") " if the port supports " (code "port-position") ", " (code "#f") " otherwise" (br) (bold "libraries: ") (code "(rnrs io ports)") ", " (code "(rnrs)")) ("A port may allow queries to determine its current position in the underlying stream of bytes or characters. If so, the procedure " (code "port-has-port-position?") " returns " (code "#t") " and " (code "port-position") " returns the current position. For binary ports, the position is always an exact nonnegative integer byte displacement from the start of the byte stream. For textual ports, the representation of a position is unspecified; it may not be an exact nonnegative integer and, even if it is, it may not represent either a byte or character displacement in the underlying stream. The position may be used at some later time to reset the position if the port supports " (code "set-port-position!") ". If " (code "port-position") " is called on a port that does not support it, an exception with condition type " (code "&assertion") " is raised.")) ("io:s50" ((bold "procedure") ": " (code "(set-port-position! " (var "port") " " (var "pos") ")") (br) (bold "returns: ") "unspecified" (br) (bold "procedure") ": " (code "(port-has-set-port-position!? " (var "port") ")") (br) (bold "returns: ") (code "#t") " if the port supports " (code "set-port-position!") ", " (code "#f") " otherwise" (br) (bold "libraries: ") (code "(rnrs io ports)") ", " (code "(rnrs)")) ("A port may allow its current position to be moved directly to a different position in the underlying stream of bytes or characters. If so, the procedure " (code "port-has-set-port-position!?") " returns " (code "#t") " and " (code "set-port-position!") " changes the current position. For binary ports, the position " (code (var "pos")) " must be an exact nonnegative integer byte displacement from the start of the byte stream. For textual ports, the representation of a position is unspecified, as described in the entry for " (code "port-position") " above, but " (code (var "pos")) " must be an appropriate position for the textual port, which is usually guaranteed to be the case only if it was obtained from a call to " (code "port-position") "  on the same port. If " (code "set-port-position!") " is called on a port that does not support it, an exception with condition type " (code "&assertion") " is raised.") ("If " (code (var "port")) " is a binary output port and the position is set beyond the current end of the data in the underlying stream, the stream is not extended until new data is written at that position. If new data is written at that position, the contents of each intervening position is unspecified. Binary ports created with " (code "open-file-output-port") " and " (code "open-file-input/output-port") " can always be extended in this manner within the limits of the underlying operating system. In other cases, attempts to set the port beyond the current end of data in the underlying object may result in an exception with condition type " (code "&i/o-invalid-position") ".")) ("io:s51" ((bold "procedure") ": " (code "(call-with-port " (var "port") " " (var "procedure") ")") (br) (bold "returns: ") "the values returned by " (code (var "procedure")) (br) (bold "libraries: ") (code "(rnrs io ports)") ", " (code "(rnrs)")) ((code "call-with-port") " calls " (code (var "procedure")) " with " (code (var "port")) " as the only argument. If " (code (var "procedure")) " returns, " (code "call-with-port") " closes the port and returns the values returned by " (code (var "procedure")) ".") ((code "call-with-port") " does not automatically close the port if a continuation created outside of " (code (var "procedure")) " is invoked, since it is possible that another continuation created inside of " (code (var "procedure")) " will be invoked at a later time, returning control to " (code (var "procedure")) ". If " (code (var "procedure")) " does not return, an implementation is free to close the port only if it can prove that the output port is no longer accessible.") ("The example below copies the contents of infile to outfile, overwriting outfile if it exists. Unless an error occurs, the ports are closed after the copy has been completed.") ((code "(call-with-port (open-file-input-port \"infile\" (file-options)" (br) "                  (buffer-mode block) (native-transcoder))" (br) "  (lambda (ip)" (br) "    (call-with-port (open-file-output-port \"outfile\"" (br) "                      (file-options no-fail)" (br) "                      (buffer-mode block)" (br) "                      (native-transcoder)) " (br) "      (lambda (op)" (br) "        (do ([c (get-char ip) (get-char ip)])" (br) "            ((eof-object? c))" (br) "          (put-char op c))))))")) ("A definition of " (code "call-with-port") " is given on page " (link "./control.html#defn:call-with-port" "135") ".")) ("io:s52" ((bold "procedure") ": " (code "(output-port-buffer-mode " (var "port") ")") (br) (bold "returns: ") "the symbol representing the buffer mode of " (code (var "port")) (br) (bold "libraries: ") (code "(rnrs io ports)") ", " (code "(rnrs)"))) ("io:s53" ((bold "procedure") ": " (code "(eof-object? " (var "obj") ")") (br) (bold "returns: ") (code "#t") " if " (code (var "obj")) " is an eof object, " (code "#f") " otherwise" (br) (bold "libraries: ") (code "(rnrs io ports)") ", " (code "(rnrs io simple)") ", " (code "(rnrs)")) ("The end-of-file object is returned by input operations, e.g., " (code "get-datum") ", when an input port has reached the end of input.")) ("io:s54" ((bold "procedure") ": " (code "(eof-object)") (br) (bold "returns: ") "the eof object" (br) (bold "libraries: ") (code "(rnrs io ports)") ", " (code "(rnrs io simple)") ", " (code "(rnrs)")) ((code "(eof-object? (eof-object)) " (math "=>") " #t"))) ("io:s55" ((bold "procedure") ": " (code "(get-u8 " (var "binary-input-port") ")") (br) (bold "returns: ") "the next byte from " (code (var "binary-input-port")) ", or the eof object" (br) (bold "libraries: ") (code "(rnrs io ports)") ", " (code "(rnrs)")) ("If " (code (var "binary-input-port")) " is at end of file, the eof object is returned. Otherwise, the next available byte is returned as an unsigned 8-bit quantity, i.e., an exact unsigned integer less than or equal to 255, and the port's position is advanced one byte.")) ("io:s56" ((bold "procedure") ": " (code "(lookahead-u8 " (var "binary-input-port") ")") (br) (bold "returns: ") "the next byte from " (code (var "binary-input-port")) ", or the eof object" (br) (bold "libraries: ") (code "(rnrs io ports)") ", " (code "(rnrs)")) ("If " (code (var "binary-input-port")) " is at end of file, the eof object is returned. Otherwise, the next available byte is returned as an unsigned 8-bit quantity, i.e., an exact unsigned integer less than or equal to 255. In contrast to " (code "get-u8") ", " (code "lookahead-u8") " does not consume the byte it reads from the port, so if the next operation on the port is a call to " (code "lookahead-u8") " or " (code "get-u8") ", the same byte is returned.")) ("io:s57" ((bold "procedure") ": " (code "(get-bytevector-n " (var "binary-input-port") " " (var "n") ")") (br) (bold "returns: ") "a nonempty bytevector containing up to " (code (var "n")) " bytes, or the eof object" (br) (bold "libraries: ") (code "(rnrs io ports)") ", " (code "(rnrs)")) ((code (var "n")) " must be an exact nonnegative integer. If " (code (var "binary-input-port")) " is at end of file, the eof object is returned. Otherwise, " (code "get-bytevector-n") " reads (as if with " (code "get-u8") ") as many bytes, up to " (code (var "n")) ", as are available before the port is at end of file, and returns a new (nonempty) bytevector containing these bytes. The port's position is advanced past the bytes read.")) ("io:s58" ((bold "procedure") ": " (code "(get-bytevector-n! " (var "binary-input-port") " " (var "bytevector") " " (var "start") " " (var "n") ")") (br) (bold "returns: ") "the count of bytes read or the eof object" (br) (bold "libraries: ") (code "(rnrs io ports)") ", " (code "(rnrs)")) ((code (var "start")) " and " (code (var "n")) " must be exact nonnegative integers, and the sum of " (code (var "start")) " and " (code (var "n")) " must not exceed the length of " (code (var "bytevector")) ".") ("If " (code (var "binary-input-port")) " is at end of file, the eof object is returned. Otherwise, " (code "get-bytevector-n!") " reads (as if with " (code "get-u8") ") as many bytes, up to " (code (var "n")) ", as are available before the port is at end of file, stores the bytes in consecutive locations of " (code (var "bytevector")) "  starting at " (code (var "start")) ", and returns the count of bytes read as an exact positive integer. The port's position is advanced past the bytes read.")) ("io:s59" ((bold "procedure") ": " (code "(get-bytevector-some " (var "binary-input-port") ")") (br) (bold "returns: ") "a nonempty bytevector or the eof object" (br) (bold "libraries: ") (code "(rnrs io ports)") ", " (code "(rnrs)")) ("If " (code (var "binary-input-port")) " is at end of file, the eof object is returned. Otherwise, " (code "get-bytevector-some") " reads (as if with " (code "get-u8") ") at least one byte and possibly more, and returns a bytevector containing these bytes. The port's position is advanced past the bytes read. The maximum number of bytes read by this operation is implementation-dependent.")) ("io:s60" ((bold "procedure") ": " (code "(get-bytevector-all " (var "binary-input-port") ")") (br) (bold "returns: ") "a nonempty bytevector or the eof object" (br) (bold "libraries: ") (code "(rnrs io ports)") ", " (code "(rnrs)")) ("If " (code (var "binary-input-port")) " is at end of file, the eof object is returned. Otherwise, " (code "get-bytevector-all") " reads (as if with " (code "get-u8") ") all of the bytes available before the port is at end of file and returns a bytevector containing these bytes. The port's position is advanced past the bytes read.")) ("io:s61" ((bold "procedure") ": " (code "(get-char " (var "textual-input-port") ")") (br) (bold "returns: ") "the next character from " (code (var "textual-input-port")) ", or the eof object" (br) (bold "libraries: ") (code "(rnrs io ports)") ", " (code "(rnrs)")) ("If " (code (var "textual-input-port")) " is at end of file, the eof object is returned. Otherwise, the next available character is returned and the port's position is advanced one character. If " (code (var "textual-input-port")) " is a transcoded port, the position in the underlying byte stream may advance by more than one byte.")) ("io:s62" ((bold "procedure") ": " (code "(lookahead-char " (var "textual-input-port") ")") (br) (bold "returns: ") "the next character from " (code (var "textual-input-port")) ", or the eof object" (br) (bold "libraries: ") (code "(rnrs io ports)") ", " (code "(rnrs)")) ("If " (code (var "textual-input-port")) " is at end of file, the eof object is returned. Otherwise, the next available character is returned. In contrast to " (code "get-char") ", " (code "lookahead-char") " does not consume the character it reads from the port, so if the next operation on the port is a call to " (code "lookahead-char") " or " (code "get-char") ", the same character is returned.") ((code "lookahead-char") " is provided for applications requiring one character of lookahead. The procedure " (code "get-word") " defined below returns the next word from a textual input port as a string, where a word is defined to be a sequence of alphabetic characters. Since " (code "get-word") " does not know until it sees one character beyond the word that it has read the entire word, it uses " (code "lookahead-char") " to determine the next character and " (code "get-char") " to consume the character.") ((code "(define get-word" (br) "  (lambda (p)" (br) "    (list->string" (br) "      (let f ()" (br) "        (let ([c (lookahead-char p)])" (br) "          (cond" (br) "            [(eof-object? c) '()]" (br) "            [(char-alphabetic? c) (get-char p) (cons c (f))]" (br) "            [else '()]))))))"))) ("io:s63" ((bold "procedure") ": " (code "(get-string-n " (var "textual-input-port") " " (var "n") ")") (br) (bold "returns: ") "a nonempty string containing up to " (code (var "n")) " characters, or the eof object" (br) (bold "libraries: ") (code "(rnrs io ports)") ", " (code "(rnrs)")) ((code (var "n")) " must be an exact nonnegative integer. If " (code (var "textual-input-port")) " is at end of file, the eof object is returned. Otherwise, " (code "get-string-n") " reads (as if with " (code "get-char") ") as many characters, up to " (code (var "n")) ", as are available before the port is at end of file, and returns a new (nonempty) string containing these characters. The port's position is advanced past the characters read.")) ("io:s64" ((bold "procedure") ": " (code "(get-string-n! " (var "textual-input-port") " " (var "string") " " (var "start") " " (var "n") ")") (br) (bold "returns: ") "the count of characters read or the eof object" (br) (bold "libraries: ") (code "(rnrs io ports)") ", " (code "(rnrs)")) ((code (var "start")) " and " (code (var "n")) " must be exact nonnegative integers, and the sum of " (code (var "start")) " and " (code (var "n")) " must not exceed the length of " (code (var "string")) ".") ("If " (code (var "textual-input-port")) " is at end of file, the eof object is returned. Otherwise, " (code "get-string-n!") " reads (as if with " (code "get-char") ") as many characters, up to " (code (var "n")) ", as are available before the port is at end of file, stores the characters in consecutive locations of " (code (var "string")) "  starting at " (code (var "start")) ", and returns the count of characters read as an exact positive integer. The port's position is advanced past the characters read.") ((code "get-string-n!") " may be used to implement " (code "string-set!") " and " (code "string-fill!") ", as illustrated below, although this is not its primary purpose.") ((code "(define string-set!" (br) "  (lambda (s i c)" (br) "    (let ([sip (open-string-input-port (string c))])" (br) "      (get-string-n! sip s i 1)" (br) "     ; return unspecified values:" (br) "      (if #f #f))))" (br) (br) "(define string-fill!" (br) "  (lambda (s c)" (br) "    (let ([n (string-length s)])" (br) "      (let ([sip (open-string-input-port (make-string n c))])" (br) "        (get-string-n! sip s 0 n)" (br) "       ; return unspecified values:" (br) "        (if #f #f)))))" (br) (br) "(let ([x (make-string 3)])" (br) "  (string-fill! x #\\-)" (br) "  (string-set! x 2 #\\))" (br) "  (string-set! x 0 #\\;)" (br) "  x) " (math "=>") " \";-)\""))) ("io:s65" ((bold "procedure") ": " (code "(get-string-all " (var "textual-input-port") ")") (br) (bold "returns: ") "a nonempty string or the eof object" (br) (bold "libraries: ") (code "(rnrs io ports)") ", " (code "(rnrs)")) ("If " (code (var "textual-input-port")) " is at end of file, the eof object is returned. Otherwise, " (code "get-string-all") " reads (as if with " (code "get-char") ") all of the characters available before the port is at end of file and returns a string containing these characters. The port's position is advanced past the characters read.")) ("io:s66" ((bold "procedure") ": " (code "(get-line " (var "textual-input-port") ")") (br) (bold "returns: ") "a string or the eof object" (br) (bold "libraries: ") (code "(rnrs io ports)") ", " (code "(rnrs)")) ("If " (code (var "textual-input-port")) " is at end of file, the eof object is returned. Otherwise, " (code "get-line") " reads (as if with " (code "get-char") ") all of the characters available before the port is at end of file or a line-feed character has been read and returns a string containing all but the line-feed character of the characters read. The port's position is advanced past the characters read.") ((code "(let ([sip (open-string-input-port \"one\\ntwo\\n\")])" (br) "  (let* ([s1 (get-line sip)] [s2 (get-line sip)])" (br) "    (list s1 s2 (port-eof? sip)))) " (math "=>") " (\"one\" \"two\" #t)" (br) (br) "(let ([sip (open-string-input-port \"one\\ntwo\")])" (br) "  (let* ([s1 (get-line sip)] [s2 (get-line sip)])" (br) "    (list s1 s2 (port-eof? sip)))) " (math "=>") " (\"one\" \"two\" #t)"))) ("io:s67" ((bold "procedure") ": " (code "(get-datum " (var "textual-input-port") ")") (br) (bold "returns: ") "a Scheme datum object or the eof object" (br) (bold "libraries: ") (code "(rnrs io ports)") ", " (code "(rnrs)")) ("This procedure scans past whitespace and comments to find the start of the external representation of a datum. If " (code (var "textual-input-port")) " reaches end of file before the start of the external representation of a datum is found, the eof object is returned.") ("Otherwise, " (code "get-datum") " reads as many characters as necessary, and no more, to parse a single datum, and returns a newly allocated object whose structure is determined by the external representation. The port's position is advanced past the characters read. If an end-of-file is reached before the external representation of the datum is complete, or an unexpected character is read, an exception is raised with condition types " (code "&lexical") " and " (code "i/o-read") ".") ((code "(let ([sip (open-string-input-port \"; a\\n\\n one (two)\\n\")])" (br) "  (let* ([x1 (get-datum sip)]" (br) "         [c1 (lookahead-char sip)]" (br) "         [x2 (get-datum sip)])" (br) "    (list x1 c1 x2 (port-eof? sip)))) " (math "=>") " (one #\\space (two) #f)"))) ("io:s68" ((bold "procedure") ": " (code "(port-eof? " (var "input-port") ")") (br) (bold "returns: ") (code "#t") " if " (code (var "input-port")) " is at end-of-file, " (code "#f") " otherwise" (br) (bold "libraries: ") (code "(rnrs io ports)") ", " (code "(rnrs)")) ("This procedure is similar to " (code "lookahead-u8") " on a binary input port or " (code "lookahead-char") " on a textual input port, except that instead of returning the next byte/character or eof object, it returns a boolean value to indicate whether the value would be the eof object.")) ("io:s69" ((bold "procedure") ": " (code "(put-u8 " (var "binary-output-port") " " (var "octet") ")") (br) (bold "returns: ") "unspecified" (br) (bold "libraries: ") (code "(rnrs io ports)") ", " (code "(rnrs)")) ((code (var "octet")) " must be an exact nonnegative integer less than or equal to 255. This procedure writes " (code (var "octet")) " to " (code (var "binary-output-port")) ", advancing the port's position by one byte.")) ("io:s70" ((bold "procedure") ": " (code "(put-bytevector " (var "binary-output-port") " " (var "bytevector") ")") (br) (bold "procedure") ": " (code "(put-bytevector " (var "binary-output-port") " " (var "bytevector") " " (var "start") ")") (br) (bold "procedure") ": " (code "(put-bytevector " (var "binary-output-port") " " (var "bytevector") " " (var "start") " " (var "n") ")") (br) (bold "returns: ") "unspecified" (br) (bold "libraries: ") (code "(rnrs io ports)") ", " (code "(rnrs)")) ((code (var "start")) " and " (code (var "n")) " must be nonnegative exact integers, and the sum of " (code (var "start")) " and " (code (var "n")) " must not exceed the length of " (code (var "bytevector")) ". If not supplied, " (code (var "start")) " defaults to zero and " (code (var "n")) " defaults to the difference between the length of " (code (var "bytevector")) " and " (code (var "start")) ".") ("This procedure writes the " (code (var "n")) " bytes of " (code (var "bytevector")) " starting at " (code (var "start")) " to the port and advances the its position past the end of the bytes written.")) ("io:s71" ((bold "procedure") ": " (code "(put-char " (var "textual-output-port") " " (var "char") ")") (br) (bold "returns: ") "unspecified" (br) (bold "libraries: ") (code "(rnrs io ports)") ", " (code "(rnrs)")) ("This procedure writes " (code (var "char")) " to " (code (var "textual-output-port")) ", advancing the port's position by one character. If " (code (var "textual-output-port")) " is a transcoded port, the position in the underlying byte stream may advance by more than one byte.")) ("io:s72" ((bold "procedure") ": " (code "(put-string " (var "textual-output-port") " " (var "string") ")") (br) (bold "procedure") ": " (code "(put-string " (var "textual-output-port") " " (var "string") " " (var "start") ")") (br) (bold "procedure") ": " (code "(put-string " (var "textual-output-port") " " (var "string") " " (var "start") " " (var "n") ")") (br) (bold "returns: ") "unspecified" (br) (bold "libraries: ") (code "(rnrs io ports)") ", " (code "(rnrs)")) ((code (var "start")) " and " (code (var "n")) " must be nonnegative exact integers, and the sum of " (code (var "start")) " and " (code (var "n")) " must not exceed the length of " (code (var "string")) ". If not supplied, " (code (var "start")) " defaults to zero and " (code (var "n")) " defaults to the difference between the length of " (code (var "string")) " and " (code (var "start")) ".") ("This procedure writes the " (code (var "n")) " characters of " (code (var "string")) " starting at " (code (var "start")) " to the port and advances the its position past the end of the characters written.")) ("io:s73" ((bold "procedure") ": " (code "(put-datum " (var "textual-output-port") " " (var "obj") ")") (br) (bold "returns: ") "unspecified" (br) (bold "libraries: ") (code "(rnrs io ports)") ", " (code "(rnrs)")) ("This procedure writes an external representation of " (code (var "obj")) " to " (code (var "textual-output-port")) ". If " (code (var "obj")) " does not have an external representation as a datum, the behavior is unspecified. The precise external representation is implementation-dependent, but when " (code (var "obj")) " does have an external representation as a datum, " (code "put-datum") " should produce a sequence of characters that can later be read by " (code "get-datum") " as an object equivalent (in the sense of " (code "equal?") ") to " (code (var "obj")) ". See Section " (link "./examples.html#g176" "12.5") " for an implementation of " (code "put-datum") ", " (code "write") ", and " (code "display") ".")) ("io:s74" ((bold "procedure") ": " (code "(flush-output-port " (var "output-port") ")") (br) (bold "returns: ") "unspecified" (br) (bold "libraries: ") (code "(rnrs io ports)") ", " (code "(rnrs)")) ("This procedure forces any bytes or characters in the buffer associated with " (code (var "output-port")) " to be sent immediately to the underlying stream.")) ("io:s75" ((bold "procedure") ": " (code "(open-input-file " (var "path") ")") (br) (bold "returns: ") "a new input port" (br) (bold "libraries: ") (code "(rnrs io simple)") ", " (code "(rnrs)")) ((code (var "path")) " must be a string or some other implementation-dependent  value that names a file. " (code "open-input-file") " creates a new textual input port for the file named by " (code (var "path")) ", as if by " (code "open-file-input-port") "  with default options, an implementation-dependent buffer mode, and an implementation-dependent transcoder.") ("The following shows the use of " (code "open-input-file") ", " (code "read") ", and " (code "close-port") " in an expression that gathers a list of objects from the file named by \"myfile.ss.\"") ((code "(let ([p (open-input-file \"myfile.ss\")])" (br) "  (let f ([x (read p)])" (br) "    (if (eof-object? x)" (br) "        (begin" (br) "          (close-port p)" (br) "          '())" (br) "        (cons x (f (read p))))))"))) ("io:s76" ((bold "procedure") ": " (code "(open-output-file " (var "path") ")") (br) (bold "returns: ") "a new output port" (br) (bold "libraries: ") (code "(rnrs io simple)") ", " (code "(rnrs)")) ((code (var "path")) " must be a string or some other implementation-dependent  value that names a file. " (code "open-output-file") " creates a new output port for the file named by " (code (var "path")) ", as if by " (code "open-file-output-port") " with default options, an implementation-dependent buffer mode, and an implementation-dependent transcoder.") ("The following shows the use of " (code "open-output-file") "  to write a list of objects (the value of " (code "list-to-be-printed") "), separated by newlines, to the file named by \"myfile.ss.\"") ((code "(let ([p (open-output-file \"myfile.ss\")])" (br) "  (let f ([ls list-to-be-printed])" (br) "    (if (not (null? ls))" (br) "        (begin" (br) "          (write (car ls) p)" (br) "          (newline p)" (br) "          (f (cdr ls)))))" (br) "  (close-port p))"))) ("io:s77" ((bold "procedure") ": " (code "(call-with-input-file " (var "path") " " (var "procedure") ")") (br) (bold "returns: ") "the values returned by " (code (var "procedure")) (br) (bold "libraries: ") (code "(rnrs io simple)") ", " (code "(rnrs)")) ((code (var "path")) " must be a string or some other implementation-dependent  value that names a file. " (code (var "procedure")) " should accept one argument.") ((code "call-with-input-file") " creates a new input port for the file named by " (code (var "path")) ", as if with " (code "open-input-file") ", and passes this port to " (code (var "procedure")) ". If " (code (var "procedure")) " returns, " (code "call-with-input-file") " closes the input port and returns the values returned by " (code (var "procedure")) ".") ((code "call-with-input-file") " does not automatically close the input port if a continuation created outside of " (code (var "procedure")) " is invoked, since it is possible that another continuation created inside of " (code (var "procedure")) " will be invoked at a later time, returning control to " (code (var "procedure")) ". If " (code (var "procedure")) " does not return, an implementation is free to close the input port only if it can prove that the input port is no longer accessible. As shown in Section " (link "./control.html#g102" "5.6") ", " (code "dynamic-wind") " may be used to ensure that the port is closed if a continuation created outside of " (code (var "procedure")) " is invoked.") ("The following example shows the use of " (code "call-with-input-file") "  in an expression that gathers a list of objects from the file named by \"myfile.ss.\" It is functionally equivalent to the example given for " (code "open-input-file") " above.") ((code "(call-with-input-file \"myfile.ss\"" (br) "  (lambda (p)" (br) "    (let f ([x (read p)])" (br) "      (if (eof-object? x)" (br) "          '()" (br) "          (cons x (f (read p)))))))")) ((code "call-with-input-file") " might be defined without error checking as follows.") ((code "(define call-with-input-file" (br) "  (lambda (filename proc)" (br) "    (let ([p (open-input-file filename)])" (br) "      (let-values ([v* (proc p)])" (br) "        (close-port p)" (br) "        (apply values v*)))))"))) ("io:s78" ((bold "procedure") ": " (code "(call-with-output-file " (var "path") " " (var "procedure") ")") (br) (bold "returns: ") "the values returned by " (code (var "procedure")) (br) (bold "libraries: ") (code "(rnrs io simple)") ", " (code "(rnrs)")) ((code (var "path")) " must be a string or some other implementation-dependent  value that names a file. " (code (var "procedure")) " should accept one argument.") ((code "call-with-output-file") " creates a new output port for the file named by " (code (var "path")) ", as if with " (code "open-output-file") ", and passes this port to " (code (var "procedure")) ". If " (code (var "procedure")) " returns, " (code "call-with-output-file") " closes the output port and returns the values returned by " (code (var "procedure")) ".") ((code "call-with-output-file") " does not automatically close the output port if a continuation created outside of " (code (var "procedure")) " is invoked, since it is possible that another continuation created inside of " (code (var "procedure")) " will be invoked at a later time, returning control to " (code (var "procedure")) ". If " (code (var "procedure")) " does not return, an implementation is free to close the output port only if it can prove that the output port is no longer accessible. As shown in Section " (link "./control.html#g102" "5.6") ", " (code "dynamic-wind") " may be used to ensure that the port is closed if a continuation created outside of " (code (var "procedure")) " is invoked.") ("The following shows the use of " (code "call-with-output-file") " to write a list of objects (the value of  " (code "list-to-be-printed") "), separated by newlines, to the file named by \"myfile.ss.\" It is functionally equivalent to the example given for " (code "open-output-file") " above.") ((code "(call-with-output-file \"myfile.ss\"" (br) "  (lambda (p)" (br) "    (let f ([ls list-to-be-printed])" (br) "      (unless (null? ls)" (br) "        (write (car ls) p)" (br) "        (newline p)" (br) "        (f (cdr ls))))))")) ((code "call-with-output-file") " might be defined without error checking as follows.") ((code "(define call-with-output-file" (br) "  (lambda (filename proc)" (br) "    (let ([p (open-output-file filename)])" (br) "      (let-values ([v* (proc p)])" (br) "        (close-port p)" (br) "        (apply values v*)))))"))) ("io:s79" ((bold "procedure") ": " (code "(with-input-from-file " (var "path") " " (var "thunk") ")") (br) (bold "returns: ") "the values returned by " (code (var "thunk")) (br) (bold "libraries: ") (code "(rnrs io simple)") ", " (code "(rnrs)")) ((code (var "path")) " must be a string or some other implementation-dependent  value that names a file. " (code (var "thunk")) " must be a procedure and should accept zero arguments.") ((code "with-input-from-file") " temporarily changes the current input port to be the result of opening the file named by " (code (var "path")) ", as if with " (code "open-input-file") ", during the application of " (code (var "thunk")) ". If " (code (var "thunk")) " returns, the port is closed and the current input port is restored to its old value.") ("The behavior of " (code "with-input-from-file") " is unspecified if a continuation created outside of " (code (var "thunk")) " is invoked before " (code (var "thunk")) " returns. An implementation may close the port and restore the current input port to its old value---but it may not.")) ("io:s80" ((bold "procedure") ": " (code "(with-output-to-file " (var "path") " " (var "thunk") ")") (br) (bold "returns: ") "the values returned by " (code (var "thunk")) (br) (bold "libraries: ") (code "(rnrs io simple)") ", " (code "(rnrs)")) ((code (var "path")) " must be a string or some other implementation-dependent  value that names a file. " (code (var "thunk")) " must be a procedure and should accept zero arguments.") ((code "with-output-to-file") " temporarily rebinds the current output port to be the result of opening the file named by " (code (var "path")) ", as if with " (code "open-output-file") ", during the application of " (code (var "thunk")) ". If " (code (var "thunk")) " returns, the port is closed and the current output port is restored to its old value.") ("The behavior of " (code "with-output-to-file") " is unspecified if a continuation created outside of " (code (var "thunk")) " is invoked before " (code (var "thunk")) " returns. An implementation may close the port and restore the current output port to its old value---but it may not.")) ("io:s81" ((bold "procedure") ": " (code "(read)") (br) (bold "procedure") ": " (code "(read " (var "textual-input-port") ")") (br) (bold "returns: ") "a Scheme datum object or the eof object" (br) (bold "libraries: ") (code "(rnrs io simple)") ", " (code "(rnrs)")) ("If " (code (var "textual-input-port")) " is not supplied, it defaults to the current input port. This procedure is otherwise equivalent to " (code "get-datum") ".")) ("io:s82" ((bold "procedure") ": " (code "(read-char)") (br) (bold "procedure") ": " (code "(read-char " (var "textual-input-port") ")") (br) (bold "returns: ") "the next character from " (code (var "textual-input-port")) (br) (bold "libraries: ") (code "