\\") " notation, as if by " (code "put-char") ". With " (code "display") ", the three-element list " (code "(a b c)") "  and the two-element list " (code "(\"a b\" c)") " both print as " (code "(a b c)") ". Because of this, " (code "display") " should not be used to print objects that are intended to be read with " (code "read") ". " (code "display") " is useful primarily for printing messages, with " (code (var "obj")) "  most often being a string. See Section " (link "./examples.html#g176" "12.5") " for an implementation of " (code "put-datum") ", " (code "write") ", and " (code "display") ".")) ("io:s86" ((bold "procedure") ": " (code "(write-char " (var "char") ")") (br) (bold "procedure") ": " (code "(write-char " (var "char") " " (var "textual-output-port") ")") (br) (bold "returns: ") "unspecified" (br) (bold "libraries: ") (code "(rnrs io simple)") ", " (code "(rnrs)")) ("If " (code (var "textual-output-port")) " is not supplied, it defaults to the current output port. This procedure is otherwise equivalent to " (code "put-char") ", with the arguments reversed.")) ("io:s87" ((bold "procedure") ": " (code "(newline)") (br) (bold "procedure") ": " (code "(newline " (var "textual-output-port") ")") (br) (bold "returns: ") "unspecified" (br) (bold "libraries: ") (code "(rnrs io simple)") ", " (code "(rnrs)")) ("If " (code (var "textual-output-port")) " is not supplied, it defaults to the current output port. " (code "newline") " sends a line-feed character to the port.")) ("io:s88" ((bold "procedure") ": " (code "(close-input-port " (var "input-port") ")") (br) (bold "procedure") ": " (code "(close-output-port " (var "output-port") ")") (br) (bold "returns: ") "unspecified" (br) (bold "libraries: ") (code "(rnrs io simple)") ", " (code "(rnrs)")) ((code "close-input-port") " closes an input port, and " (code "close-output-port") " closes an output port. These procedures are provided for backward compatibility with the Revised" (sup "5") "  Report; they are not actually more convenient to use than " (code "close-port") ".")) ("io:s89" ((bold "procedure") ": " (code "(file-exists? " (var "path") ")") (br) (bold "returns: ") (code "#t") " if the file named by " (code (var "path")) " exists, " (code "#f") " otherwise" (br) (bold "libraries: ") (code "(rnrs files)") ", " (code "(rnrs)")) ((code (var "path")) " must be a string or some other implementation-dependent  value that names a file. Whether " (code "file-exists?") " follows symbolic links is unspecified.")) ("io:s90" ((bold "procedure") ": " (code "(delete-file " (var "path") ")") (br) (bold "returns: ") "unspecified" (br) (bold "libraries: ") (code "(rnrs files)") ", " (code "(rnrs)")) ((code (var "path")) " must be a string or some other implementation-dependent  value that names a file. " (code "delete-file") " removes the file named by " (code (var "path")) " if it exists and can be deleted, otherwise it raises an exception with condition type " (code "&i/o-filename") ". Whether " (code "delete-file") " follows symbolic links is unspecified.")) ("io:s91" ((bold "procedure") ": " (code "(bytevector->string " (var "bytevector") " " (var "transcoder") ")") (br) (bold "returns: ") "a string containing the characters encoded in " (code (var "bytevector")) (br) (bold "libraries: ") (code "(rnrs io ports)") ", " (code "(rnrs)")) ("This operation, at least in effect, creates a bytevector input port with the specified " (code (var "transcoder")) " from which all of the available characters are read, as if by " (code "get-string-all") ", and placed into the output string.") ((code "(let ([tx (make-transcoder (utf-8-codec) (eol-style lf)" (br) "            (error-handling-mode replace))])" (br) "  (bytevector->string #vu8(97 98 99) tx)) " (math "=>") " \"abc\""))) ("io:s92" ((bold "procedure") ": " (code "(string->bytevector " (var "string") " " (var "transcoder") ")") (br) (bold "returns: ") "a bytevector containing the encodings of the characters in " (code (var "string")) (br) (bold "libraries: ") (code "(rnrs io ports)") ", " (code "(rnrs)")) ("This operation, at least in effect, creates a bytevector output port with the specified " (code (var "transcoder")) " to which all of the characters of " (code (var "string")) " are written, then extracts a bytevector containing the accumulated bytes.") ((code "(let ([tx (make-transcoder (utf-8-codec) (eol-style none)" (br) "            (error-handling-mode raise))])" (br) "  (string->bytevector \"abc\" tx)) " (math "=>") " #vu8(97 98 99)"))) ("io:s93" ((bold "procedure") ": " (code "(string->utf8 " (var "string") ")") (br) (bold "returns: ") "a bytevector containing the UTF-8 encoding of " (code (var "string")) (br) (bold "libraries: ") (code "(rnrs bytevectors)") ", " (code "(rnrs)"))) ("io:s94" ((bold "procedure") ": " (code "(string->utf16 " (var "string") ")") (br) (bold "procedure") ": " (code "(string->utf16 " (var "string") " " (var "endianness") ")") (br) (bold "procedure") ": " (code "(string->utf32 " (var "string") ")") (br) (bold "procedure") ": " (code "(string->utf32 " (var "string") " " (var "endianness") ")") (br) (bold "returns: ") "a bytevector containing the specified encoding of " (code (var "string")) (br) (bold "libraries: ") (code "(rnrs bytevectors)") ", " (code "(rnrs)")) ((code (var "endianness")) " must be one of the symbols " (code "big") " or " (code "little") ". If " (code (var "endianness")) " is not provided or is the symbol " (code "big") ", " (code "string->utf16") " returns the UTF-16BE encoding of " (code (var "string")) " and " (code "string->utf32") " returns the UTF-32BE encoding of " (code (var "string")) ". If " (code (var "endianness")) " is the symbol " (code "little") ", " (code "string->utf16") " returns the UTF-16LE encoding of " (code (var "string")) " and " (code "string->utf32") " returns the UTF-32LE encoding of " (code (var "string")) ". No byte-order mark is included in the encoding.")) ("io:s95" ((bold "procedure") ": " (code "(utf8->string " (var "bytevector") ")") (br) (bold "returns: ") "a string containing the UTF-8 decoding of " (code (var "bytevector")) (br) (bold "libraries: ") (code "(rnrs bytevectors)") ", " (code "(rnrs)"))) ("io:s96" ((bold "procedure") ": " (code "(utf16->string " (var "bytevector") " " (var "endianness") ")") (br) (bold "procedure") ": " (code "(utf16->string " (var "bytevector") " " (var "endianness") " " (var "endianness-mandatory?") ")") (br) (bold "procedure") ": " (code "(utf32->string " (var "bytevector") " " (var "endianness") ")") (br) (bold "procedure") ": " (code "(utf32->string " (var "bytevector") " " (var "endianness") " " (var "endianness-mandatory?") ")") (br) (bold "returns: ") "a string containing the specified decoding of " (code (var "bytevector")) (br) (bold "libraries: ") (code "(rnrs bytevectors)") ", " (code "(rnrs)")) ((code (var "endianness")) " must be one of the symbols " (code "big") " or " (code "little") ". These procedures return a UTF-16 or UTF-32 decoding of " (code (var "bytevector")) ", with the endianness of the representation determined from the endianness argument or byte-order mark (BOM). If " (code (var "endianness-mandatory?")) " is not provided or is " (code "#f") ", the endianness is determined by a BOM at the front of " (code (var "bytevector")) " or, if no BOM is present, by " (code (var "endianness")) ". If " (code (var "endianness-mandatory?")) " is " (code "#t") ", the endianness is determined by " (code (var "endianness")) ", and, if a BOM appears at the front of " (code (var "bytevector")) ", it is treated as a regular character encoding.") ("The UTF-16 BOM is the two-byte sequence " (code "#xFE") ", " (code "#xFF") "  specifying \"big\" or the two-byte sequence " (code "#xFF") ", " (code "#xFE") "  specifying \"little.\" The UTF-32 BOM is the four-byte sequence " (code "#x00") ", " (code "#x00") ", " (code "#xFE") ", " (code "#xFF") " specifying \"big\" or the four-byte sequence " (code "#xFF") ", " (code "#xFE") ", " (cod