ments. For example, " (code "string>?") " determines if the lexicographic ordering of its arguments is monotonically decreasing.") ("The comparisons are based on the character predicates " (code "char=?") "  and " (code "char<?") ". Two strings are lexicographically equivalent if they are the same length and consist of the same sequence of characters according to " (code "char=?") ". If two strings differ only in length, the shorter string is considered to be lexicographically less than the longer string. Otherwise, the first character position at which the strings differ (by " (code "char=?") ") determines which string is lexicographically less than the other, according to " (code "char<?") ".") ("Two-argument " (code "string=?") " may be defined without error checks as follows.") ((code "(define string=?" (br) "  (lambda (s1 s2)" (br) "    (let ([n (string-length s1)])" (br) "      (and (= (string-length s2) n)" (br) "           (let loop ([i 0])" (br) "             (or (= i n)" (br) "                 (and (char=? (string-ref s1 i) (string-ref s2 i))" (br) "                      (loop (+ i 1)))))))))")) ("Two-argument " (code "string<?") " may be defined without error checks as follows.") ((code "(define string<?" (br) "  (lambda (s1 s2)" (br) "    (let ([n1 (string-length s1)] [n2 (string-length s2)])" (br) "      (let loop ([i 0])" (br) "        (and (not (= i n2))" (br) "             (or (= i n1)" (br) "                 (let ([c1 (string-ref s1 i)] [c2 (string-ref s2 i)])" (br) "                   (or (char<? c1 c2)" (br) "                       (and (char=? c1 c2)" (br) "                            (loop (+ i 1)))))))))))")) ("These definitions may be extended straightforwardly to support three or more arguments. " (code "string<=?") ", " (code "string>?") ", and " (code "string>=?") "  may be defined similarly.") ((code "(string=? \"mom\" \"mom\") " (math "=>") " #t" (br) "(string<? \"mom\" \"mommy\") " (math "=>") " #t" (br) "(string>? \"Dad\" \"Dad\") " (math "=>") " #f" (br) "(string=? \"Mom and Dad\" \"mom and dad\") " (math "=>") " #f" (br) "(string<? \"a\" \"b\" \"c\") " (math "=>") " #t"))) ("objects:s216" ((bold "procedure") ": " (code "(string-ci=? " (var "string" (sub "1")) " " (var "string" (sub "2")) " " (var "string" (sub "3")) " ...)") (br) (bold "procedure") ": " (code "(string-ci<? " (var "string" (sub "1")) " " (var "string" (sub "2")) " " (var "string" (sub "3")) " ...)") (br) (bold "procedure") ": " (code "(string-ci>? " (var "string" (sub "1")) " " (var "string" (sub "2")) " " (var "string" (sub "3")) " ...)") (br) (bold "procedure") ": " (code "(string-ci<=? " (var "string" (sub "1")) " " (var "string" (sub "2")) " " (var "string" (sub "3")) " ...)") (br) (bold "procedure") ": " (code "(string-ci>=? " (var "string" (sub "1")) " " (var "string" (sub "2")) " " (var "string" (sub "3")) " ...)") (br) (bold "returns: ") (code "#t") " if the relation holds, " (code "#f") " otherwise" (br) (bold "libraries: ") (code "(rnrs unicode)") ", " (code "(rnrs)")) ("These predicates are identical to " (code "string=?") ", " (code "string<?") ", " (code "string>?") ", " (code "string<=?") ", and " (code "string>=?") " except that they are case-insensitive, i.e., compare the case-folded versions of their arguments.") ((code "(string-ci=? \"Mom and Dad\" \"mom and dad\") " (math "=>") " #t" (br) "(string-ci<=? \"say what\" \"Say What!?\") " (math "=>") " #t" (br) "(string-ci>? \"N\" \"m\" \"L\" \"k\") " (math "=>") " #t" (br) "(string-ci=? \"Straße\" \"Strasse\") " (math "=>") " #t"))) ("objects:s217" ((bold "procedure") ": " (code "(string " (var "char") " ...)") (br) (bold "returns: ") "a string containing the characters " (code (var "char") " ...") (br) (bold "libraries: ") (code "(rnrs base)") ", " (code "(rnrs)")) ((code "(string) " (math "=>") " \"\"" (br) "(string #\\a #\\b #\\c) " (math "=>") " \"abc\"" (br) "(string #\\H #\\E #\\Y #\\!) " (math "=>") " \"HEY!\""))) ("objects:s218" ((bold "procedure") ": " (code "(make-string " (var "n") ")") (br) (bold "procedure") ": " (code "(make-string " (var "n") " " (var "char") ")") (br) (bold "returns: ") "a string of length " (code (var "n")) (br) (bold "libraries: ") (code "(rnrs base)") ", " (code "(rnrs)")) ((code (var "n")) " must be an exact nonnegative integer. If " (code (var "char")) " is supplied, the string is filled with " (code (var "n")) "  occurrences of " (code (var "char")) ", otherwise the characters contained in the string are unspecified.") ((code "(make-string 0) " (math "=>") " \"\"" (br) "(make-string 0 #\\x) " (math "=>") " \"\"" (br) "(make-string 5 #\\x) " (math "=>") " \"xxxxx\""))) ("objects:s219" ((bold "procedure") ": " (code "(string-length " (var "string") ")") (br) (bold "returns: ") "the number of characters in " (code (var "string")) (br) (bold "libraries: ") (code "(rnrs base)") ", " (code "(rnrs)")) ("The length of a string is always an exact nonnegative integer.") ((code "(string-length \"abc\") " (math "=>") " 3" (br) "(string-length \"\") " (math "=>") " 0" (br) "(string-length \"hi there\") " (math "=>") " 8" (br) "(string-length (make-string 1000000)) " (math "=>") " 1000000"))) ("objects:s220" ((bold "procedure") ": " (code "(string-ref " (var "string") " " (var "n") ")") (br) (bold "returns: ") "the " (code (var "n")) "th character (zero-based) of " (code (var "string")) (br) (bold "libraries: ") (code "(rnrs base)") ", " (code "(rnrs)")) ((code (var "n")) " must be an exact nonnegative integer less than the length of " (code (var "string")) ".") ((code "(string-ref \"hi there\" 0) " (math "=>") " #\\h" (br) "(string-ref \"hi there\" 5) " (math "=>") " #\\e"))) ("objects:s221" ((bold "procedure") ": " (code "(string-set! " (var "string") " " (var "n") " " (var "char") ")") (br) (bold "returns: ") "unspecified" (br) (bold "libraries: ") (code "(rnrs mutable-strings)")) ((code (var "n")) " must be an exact nonnegative integer less than the length of " (code (var "string")) ". " (code "st