of " (code (var "string")) " from " (code (var "start")) " (inclusive) to " (code (var "end")) "  (exclusive)" (br) (bold "libraries: ") (code "(rnrs base)") ", " (code "(rnrs)")) ((code (var "start")) " and " (code (var "end")) " must be exact nonnegative integers; " (code (var "start")) " must be less than or equal to " (code (var "end")) ", while " (code (var "end")) " must be less than or equal to the length of " (code (var "string")) ". If " (code (var "end")) " = " (code (var "start")) ", a string of length zero is returned. " (code "substring") " may be defined without error checks as follows.") ((code "(define substring" (br) "  (lambda (s1 m n)" (br) "    (let ([s2 (make-string (- n m))])" (br) "      (do ([j 0 (+ j 1)] [i m (+ i 1)])" (br) "          ((= i n) s2)" (br) "        (string-set! s2 j (string-ref s1 i))))))" (br) (br) "(substring \"hi there\" 0 1) " (math "=>") " \"h\"" (br) "(substring \"hi there\" 3 6) " (math "=>") " \"the\"" (br) "(substring \"hi there\" 5 5) " (math "=>") " \"\"" (br) (br) "(let ([str \"hi there\"])" (br) "  (let ([end (string-length str)])" (br) "    (substring str 0 end))) " (math "=>") " \"hi there\""))) ("objects:s225" ((bold "procedure") ": " (code "(string-fill! " (var "string") " " (var "char") ")") (br) (bold "returns: ") "unspecified" (br) (bold "libraries: ") (code "(rnrs mutable-strings)")) ((code "string-fill!") " sets every character in " (code (var "string")) " to " (code (var "char")) ".") ((code "(let ([str (string-copy \"sleepy\")])" (br) "  (string-fill! str #\\Z)" (br) "  str) " (math "=>") " \"ZZZZZZ\"")) ((code "string-fill!") " might be defined as follows:") ((code "(define string-fill!" (br) "  (lambda (s c)" (br) "    (let ([n (string-length s)])" (br) "      (do ([i 0 (+ i 1)])" (br) "          ((= i n))" (br) "          (string-set! s i c)))))")) ("An alternative definition is given on page " (link "./io.html#backdoor-string-fill" "276") ".")) ("objects:s226" ((bold "procedure") ": " (code "(string-upcase " (var "string") ")") (br) (bold "returns: ") "the upper-case equivalent of " (code (var "string")) (br) (bold "procedure") ": " (code "(string-downcase " (var "string") ")") (br) (bold "returns: ") "the lower-case equivalent of " (code (var "string")) (br) (bold "procedure") ": " (code "(string-foldcase " (var "string") ")") (br) (bold "returns: ") "the case-folded equivalent of " (code (var "string")) (br) (bold "procedure") ": " (code "(string-titlecase " (var "string") ")") (br) (bold "returns: ") "the title-case equivalent of " (code (var "string")) (br) (bold "libraries: ") (code "(rnrs unicode)") ", " (code "(rnrs)")) ("These procedures implement Unicode's locale-independent case mappings from scalar-value sequences to scalar-value sequences. These mappings do not always map single characters to single characters, so the length of the result string may differ from the length of " (code (var "string")) ". If the result string is the same as " (code (var "string")) " (by " (code "string=?") "), " (code (var "string")) " or a copy of " (code (var "string")) " may be returned. Otherwise, the result string is newly allocated. " (code "string-foldcase") " does not use the special mappings for Turkic languages.") ((code "string-titlecase") " converts the first cased character of each word in " (code (var "string")) " to its title-case counterpart and converts each other character to its lower-case counterpart. Word breaks are recognized as specified in Unicode Standard Annex #29 [" (link "./bibliography.html#g226" "8") "].") ((code "(string-upcase \"Hi\") " (math "=>") " \"HI\"" (br) "(string-downcase \"Hi\") " (math "=>") " \"hi\"" (br) "(string-foldcase \"Hi\") " (math "=>") " \"hi\"" (br) (br) "(string-upcase \"Straße\") " (math "=>") " \"STRASSE\"" (br) "(string-downcase \"Straße\") " (math "=>") " \"straße\"" (br) "(string-foldcase \"Straße\") " (math "=>") " \"strasse\"" (br) "(string-downcase \"STRASSE\")  " (math "=>") " \"strasse\"" (br) (br) "(stri