unspecified" (br) (bold "libraries: ") (code "(rnrs hashtables)") ", " (code "(rnrs)")) ((code (var "hashtable")) " must be a mutable hashtable. If " (code (var "size")) " is provided, it must be a nonnegative exact integer.") ((code "hashtable-clear!") " removes all entries from " (code (var "hashtable")) ". If size is provided, the hashtable is reset to the given size, as if newly created by one of the hashtable creation operations with size argument " (code (var "size")) ".") ((code "(define ht (make-eq-hashtable))" (br) "(define p1 (cons 'a 'b))" (br) "(define p2 (cons 'a 'b))" (br) "(hashtable-set! ht p1 \"first\")" (br) "(hashtable-set! ht p2 \"second\")" (br) "(hashtable-size ht) " (math "=>") " 2" (br) "(hashtable-clear! ht)" (br) "(hashtable-size ht) " (math "=>") " 0" (br) "(hashtable-ref ht p1 #f) " (math "=>") " #f"))) ("objects:s288" ((bold "procedure") ": " (code "(hashtable-keys " (var "hashtable") ")") (br) (bold "returns: ") "a vector containing the keys in " (code (var "hashtable")) (br) (bold "libraries: ") (code "(rnrs hashtables)") ", " (code "(rnrs)")) ("The keys may appear in any order in the returned vector.") ((code "(define ht (make-eq-hashtable))" (br) "(define p1 (cons 'a 'b))" (br) "(define p2 (cons 'a 'b))" (br) "(hashtable-set! ht p1 \"one\")" (br) "(hashtable-set! ht p2 \"two\")" (br) "(hashtable-set! ht 'q \"three\")" (br) "(hashtable-keys ht) " (math "=>") " #((a . b) q (a . b))"))) ("objects:s289" ((bold "procedure") ": " (code "(hashtable-entries " (var "hashtable") ")") (br) (bold "returns: ") "two vectors: one of keys and a second of values" (br) (bold "libraries: ") (code "(rnrs hashtables)") ", " (code "(rnrs)")) ((code "hashtable-entries") " returns two values. The first is a vector containing the keys in " (code (var "hashtable")) ", and the second is a vector containing the corresponding values. The keys and values may appear in any order, but the order is the same for the keys and for the corresponding values.") ((code "(define ht (make-eq-hashtable))" (br) "(define p1 (cons 'a 'b))" (br) "(define p2 (cons 'a 'b))" (br) "(hashtable-set! ht p1 \"one\")" (br) "(hashtable-set! ht p2 \"two\")" (br) "(hashtable-set! ht 'q \"three\")" (br) "(hashtable-entries ht) " (math "=>") " #((a . b) q (a . b))" (br) "                       " (math "  ") " #(\"two\" \"three\" \"one\")"))) ("objects:s290" ((bold "syntax") ": " (code "(define-enumeration " (var "name") " (" (var "symbol") " ...) " (var "constructor") ")") (br) (bold "libraries: ") (code "(rnrs enums)") ", " (code "(rnrs)")) ("A " (code "define-enumeration") " form is a definition and can appear anywhere any other definition can appear.") ("The " (code "define-enumeration") " syntax creates a new enumeration set with the specified symbols in the specified order forming the enumeration's universe. It defines a new syntactic form named by " (code (var "name")) " that may be used to verify that a symbol is in the universe. If " (code (var "x")) " is in the universe, " (code "(" (var "name " (var "x")) ")") " evaluates to " (code (var "x")) ". It is a syntax violation if " (code (var "x")) " is not in the universe.") ((code "define-enumeration") " also defines a new syntactic form named by " (code (var "constructor")) " that may be used to create subsets of the enumeration type. If " (code (var "x") " ...") " are each in the universe, " (code (var "(constructor " (var "x")) " ...)") " evaluates to an enumeration set containing " (code (var "x") " ...") ". Otherwise, it is a syntax violation. The same symbol may appear more than once in " (code (var "x") " ...") ", but the resulting set contains only one occurrence of the symbol.") ((code "(define-enumeration weather-element" (br) "  (hot warm cold sunny rainy snowy windy)" (br) "  weather)" (br) (br) "(weather-element hot) " (math "=>") " hot" (br) "(weather-element fun) " (math "=>") " " (var "syntax violation") (br) "(weather hot sunny windy) " (math "=>") " #<enum-set>" (br) "(enum-set->l